__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Raw sweep arrays are large and regenerable from the scripts; the FIGURES are committed
# so the result is visible without a GPU (see results/figures/ and RESULTS.md).
results/*.npz

# P1-E7 IS THE EXCEPTION, because "regenerable" stopped being true for it. Its `attacked`
# and `control` stages are LoRA merges that existed only on a rented pod, and that pod is
# gone. Re-running attack.py does not reproduce them -- it trains a NEW checkpoint, whose
# numbers would be a replication rather than these numbers. So these files are primary
# evidence for every figure in the P1-E7 sections of RESULTS.md, and losing the one laptop
# holding them would make the experiment unreproducible.
#
# Only the small ones: 0.9 MB for all twelve. The three *_probe.npz are 22.5 MB each because
# they carry `directions` and `null_directions` in full; they are needed only to re-run a
# transplant with a different source, not to reproduce anything already reported.
!results/olmo2_e7_*_refusal.npz
!results/olmo2_e7_*_transfer.npz
!results/olmo2_e7_*_transplant.npz
!results/olmo2_e7_*_transplant-induce.npz

# The run ledger IS the experimental record and is COMMITTED — it answers "which code
# produced this number, when, on what hardware", and a ledger that dies with the pod
# answers nothing. Small, append-only text; merge conflicts here are expected and are
# resolved by keeping BOTH sides (two machines ran two experiments).
!results/runs.jsonl
!results/RUNLOG.md

data/xstest_prompts.csv

# P1-E7 attacked checkpoints: ~15 GB each, regenerable from attack_manifest.json
models/

# `script(1)` transcript — created when a terminal-capture command misfires on a pod.
# One got committed on 2026-09-19 (empty, harmless, but noise in the tree).
typescript

# P1-E7z / P1-E7g: small (~0.5 MB for six models) and they hold the only copy of the steered
# generations. Regenerating them needs the endpoint adapters, which exist in one tarball on one
# laptop (O-187) -- "regenerable" is not true enough to leave them out.
!results/p1e7z_*.npz
!results/p1e7g_*.npz
